<v Ira Glass>Knowing What We Know-- so if you're following the news at all, you know that Huma Abedin, one of Hillary Clinton's top aides, is married to former congressman Anthony Weiner who just this week reportedly checked himself into a sex addiction clinic. Because after two public apologies when he was caught sending pictures of his crotch to random women online, he then went on to send a crotch shot to a 15-year-old girl and allegedly had a whole online sexual relationship with that girl.
<v Ira Glass>知情——如果你一直在关注新闻，你就知道希拉里·克林顿的高级助手之一胡玛·阿贝丁嫁给了前国会议员安东尼·韦纳，据报道，就在本周，他自己住进了性瘾诊所。因为在两次公开道歉后，他被抓到在网上给随机女性发送裤裆照片，随后又给一名15岁女孩发送了裤裆照片，并据称与该女孩有了一段完整的在线性关系。

00:29:16.970 --> 00:29:43.330
<v Ira Glass>That triggered investigation. And as you probably know, his laptop and phone were seized. And then, while authorities were looking on his computer, they found e-mails between Weiner's wife, Huma Abedin, and Hillary Clinton. And those e-mails, of course, are what led the FBI to investigate another round of Clinton e-mails. And that, of course, is what led to the dramatic drop in Clinton's poll numbers and, incidentally, to Donald Trump saying, thank you, Huma. Good job, Huma.
<v Ira Glass>这引发了调查。正如你可能知道的那样，他的笔记本电脑和手机被查封。然后，当当局在他的电脑上查看时，发现了韦纳的妻子胡玛·阿贝丁与希拉里·克林顿之间的电子邮件。当然，正是这些电子邮件导致FBI调查了另一轮克林顿的电子邮件。当然，这导致了克林顿民调数据的急剧下降，顺便说一句，唐纳德·特朗普说，谢谢，胡玛。干得好，胡玛。

00:29:43.330 --> 00:30:04.290
<v Ira Glass>If there's one person in the world who might understand what it's like for Huma Abedin to be a public figure and a woman repeatedly paying a public price for her husband's extramarital sex life-- she's in luck-- the one person in the world who might understand this best is probably her boss, Hillary Clinton. What is it like when they talk about this?
<v Ira Glass>如果世界上有一个人可能理解胡玛·阿贝丁作为一个公众人物，一个女人为了丈夫婚外性生活而一再付出公开代价是什么感觉——她很幸运——世界上最能理解这一点的人可能是她的老板，希拉里·克林顿。她们谈论这件事时是什么样子？

00:30:04.290 --> 00:30:28.960
<v Ira Glass>OK, obviously, they're not going to do it over e-mail. This requires face-to-face conversation. This then is the conversation that we imagine they had last Friday. That's the day the news broke that Weiner's laptop-- because of his lap-- would change the focus and direction of the presidential election. Or should I say the presidential-- never mind. This, then, is the first conversation they have with that news hanging between them.
<v Ira Glass>好吧，显然她们不会通过电子邮件谈论。这需要面对面的交谈。这便是我们想象中她们上周五进行的对话。那是韦纳的笔记本电脑——因为他的笔记本电脑——将改变总统选举的焦点和方向的那一天。或者我应该说总统的……没关系。这就是她们在那个新闻悬而未决的情况下进行的第一次谈话。

